  "asr_text": "The person who leaves a delivery notice, the person who comes back and sees it, and the person who stops by a locker all want fewer redeliveries. What matters to them is different: money going to the people delivering packages, the promise of waiting for a morning delivery, and how the effort of going to a locker is rewarded. They disagree on whether people who are repeatedly out should pay or whether the cost should be covered by the overall shipping fee. Packages that don't arrive in the morning and packages that can't be sent to lockers are problems the person receiving them can't solve through their own efforts alone. On the day your next package is supposed to arrive, where will you be and what will you be doing while you wait?",
